===Etymology===
From {{m|fi|mäntä||archaic: mixing utensil made of the top of a young pine}}; cognate of Estonian {{m|fi|mänd}}; originally the word meant a young pine, and now relatively rare words {{m|fi|petäjä}} and {{m|fi|honka}} were used of the older trees.

